<title>FRANCE: Remy eyeing possible drink opportunities.</title>
<headline>Remy eyeing possible drink opportunities.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Remy-Cointreau said on Wednesday it may be interested in drink brands up for sale as the result of a planned merger of the drinks businesses of Guinness Plc and Grand Metropolitan Plc and maybe LVMH Moet Hennessy Louis Vuitton.</p>
<p>&quot;Whatever the outcome of the linkup between the two or three groups, our distribution network could benefit from opportunities,&quot; managing director Marc Heriard Dubreuil told reporters.</p>
<p>Guinness and Grand Met announced plans to merge in May. LVMH, the biggest shareholder in both companies, opposes their merger plan and is trying to push them to consider its proposal to set up a stand-alone, listed drinks business.</p>
<p>Share analysts said either scenario would probably require some brand disposals to satisfy competition authorities.</p>
<p>((-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452))</p>
